# Update-system metadata is signed over its exact bytes.
#
# git is a canonicaliser: with core.autocrlf=true it rewrites CRLF to LF on commit, which
# once made the served channel.json 26 bytes shorter than the file that had been signed.
# Every launcher then correctly rejected the release as tampered with.
#
# -text tells git never to touch line endings in these paths, so what is signed is what is
# committed is what raw.githubusercontent.com serves. The publisher also emits LF, so this
# is the second of two independent guards rather than the only one.

channels/**    -text
manifests/**   -text
*.sig          -text
